---
import { getPublishedCollection } from "astro-course-university/content";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
import Callout from "astro-theme-university/components/Callout.astro";
import CourseLayout from "../../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import { formatCourseDate } from "../../../lib/dates";

const assessments = (await getPublishedCollection("assessments")).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.week - b.data.week,
);
const convenorEmail = "marisol.quaye@slop.university";

const options = assessments.map((assessment) => ({
  id: assessment.id,
  title: assessment.data.title,
  due: assessment.data.due.toISOString().slice(0, 10),
  dueLabel: formatCourseDate(assessment.data.due),
  weight: assessment.data.weight,
}));
---

<CourseLayout
  title="Extensions"
  description="What an extension is for on a course about restraint, what it will not buy you, and how to ask for one before the due date rather than after it."
>
  <p>
    A course that spends twelve weeks arguing that leaving things out is a discipline has an
    awkward relationship with the word <em>extension</em>. More time is more material, and more
    material is the failure mode this syllabus was built to resist. So the rule here is narrower
    than the university's default: an extension buys you time to make the same cut properly, not
    time to put back in what you should have removed.
  </p>

  <Callout type="warning">
    <p>
      <strong>Ask before the due date.</strong> A request that arrives after the deadline is a
      late-penalty appeal, not an extension, and it goes through the university's process rather
      than this one.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>What counts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Illness or injury</strong>, yours or someone you care for, covering any part of the
      working period — not only the final week.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Circumstances outside your control</strong>: bereavement, displacement, a job that
      moved without notice, a carer's week that arrived unannounced.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A medium that failed you</strong>. A studio piece whose material, equipment or
      collaborator fell through is a real obstruction, and this course marks the piece, not your
      luck with a borrowed camera.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What does not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Scope you chose.</strong> A piece that has grown past what the brief asked for is
      not running late; it is running long, and the fix is the course's own subject.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Wanting another pass.</strong> Every piece would be better with one more week. The
      deadline is the cut, and the cut is the assessment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Three assessments landing near each other.</strong> They land where the
      <a href={withBase("/modules/")}>module schedule</a> says they will, from week one.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long you can ask for</h2>
  <p>
    Up to seven days is decided by the convenor and usually answered within two working days.
    Beyond seven days the request goes to the school, needs documentation, and — on a
    twelve-week course — starts to collide with the next piece of work. If you need more than a
    fortnight, the conversation to have is about deferral, not extension.
  </p>

  <h2>Draft your request</h2>
  <p>
    Fill this in and it composes the email for you, with the fields the convenor otherwise has to
    ask for. Nothing is sent until you press send in your own mail client.
  </p>

  <form class="ext-form" id="ext-form" data-convenor={convenorEmail}>
    <div class="ext-field">
      <label for="ext-assessment">Which assessment</label>
      <select id="ext-assessment" name="assessment">
        {
          options.map((option) => (
            <option value={option.id} data-due={option.due} data-due-label={option.dueLabel}>
              {option.title} — due {option.dueLabel} ({option.weight}%)
            </option>
          ))
        }
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="ext-field">
      <label for="ext-days">Days requested</label>
      <select id="ext-days" name="days">
        <option value="2">2 days</option>
        <option value="4">4 days</option>
        <option value="7" selected>7 days (the convenor's limit)</option>
        <option value="14">14 days (goes to the school)</option>
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="ext-field">
      <label for="ext-reason">Grounds</label>
      <select id="ext-reason" name="reason">
        <option value="illness or injury affecting the working period">Illness or injury</option>
        <option value="caring responsibilities that arrived without notice">Caring responsibilities</option>
        <option value="bereavement or another serious personal circumstance">Bereavement or personal circumstance</option>
        <option value="a material, equipment or collaborator failure in the studio work">Studio or equipment failure</option>
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="ext-field">
      <label for="ext-detail">What happened, in a sentence or two</label>
      <textarea id="ext-detail" name="detail" rows="3" placeholder="The specifics, not the category — the convenor is reading for whether the obstruction was real, not whether it sounds serious."></textarea>
    </div>

    <div class="ext-field">
      <label for="ext-name">Your name and student number</label>
      <input id="ext-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" />
    </div>

    <p class="ext-new-due">
      New due date if granted: <strong data-ext-newdue>—</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      <a class="ext-send" href={`mailto:${convenorEmail}`} data-ext-mailto>Open this in your mail client</a>
    </p>
    <p class="ext-note">
      This form builds a <code>mailto:</code> link in your browser. It stores nothing and submits
      nothing; the site has no server to submit it to.
    </p>
  </form>

  <h2>After it is granted</h2>
  <p>
    An extension moves the due date and nothing else. The rubric on the assessment page is the
    same rubric, the weight is the same weight, and the marker will not know — nor should they —
    that the piece arrived a week later than the rest. What you have bought is room to finish the
    cut, and the cut is still the thing being marked.
  </p>
</CourseLayout>

<script>
  function bindExtensionForm() {
    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>("#ext-form");
    if (!form) return;
    const convenor = form.dataset.convenor ?? "";
    const assessment = form.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#ext-assessment");
    const days = form.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#ext-days");
    const reason = form.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#ext-reason");
    const detail = form.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("#ext-detail");
    const name = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#ext-name");
    const newDue = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-ext-newdue]");
    const mailto = form.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>("[data-ext-mailto]");
    if (!assessment || !days || !reason || !detail || !name || !newDue || !mailto) return;

    const formatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-AU", { dateStyle: "long", timeZone: "UTC" });

    function update() {
      const option = assessment!.selectedOptions[0];
      const due = option?.dataset.due ?? "";
      const dueLabel = option?.dataset.dueLabel ?? due;
      const added = Number(days!.value);
      const moved = new Date(due + "T00:00:00Z");
      moved.setUTCDate(moved.getUTCDate() + added);
      const movedLabel = formatter.format(moved);
      newDue!.textContent = movedLabel;

      const subject =
        "SLOP3268 extension request: " + (option?.textContent ?? "").split(" — ")[0];
      const body = [
        "Dear Marisol,",
        "",
        "I am asking for a " + added + "-day extension on " +
          (option?.textContent ?? "").split(" — ")[0] + ", currently due " + dueLabel + ".",
        "",
        "Grounds: " + reason!.value + ".",
        "",
        detail!.value.trim() || "[what happened, in a sentence or two]",
        "",
        "If granted, the new due date would be " + movedLabel + ".",
        "",
        name!.value.trim() || "[your name and student number]",
      ].join("\n");

      mailto!.href =
        "mailto:" + convenor + "?subject=" + encodeURIComponent(subject) +
        "&body=" + encodeURIComponent(body);
    }

    for (const field of [assessment, days, reason, detail, name]) {
      field.addEventListener("input", update);
    }
    form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => event.preventDefault());
    update();
  }

  bindExtensionForm();
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", bindExtensionForm);
</script>

<style>
  .ext-form {
    margin-block: var(--at-spacing-lg);
    padding: var(--at-spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    border-inline-start: 4px solid var(--at-accent);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
  }

  .ext-field {
    margin-block-end: var(--at-spacing-md);
  }

  .ext-field label {
    display: block;
    margin-block-end: var(--at-spacing-xs);
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .ext-field select,
  .ext-field input,
  .ext-field textarea {
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--at-border);
    border-radius: var(--at-border-radius);
    background: var(--at-bg);
    color: var(--at-text);
  }

  .ext-field :is(select, input, textarea):focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--at-accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }

  .ext-new-due {
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
  }

  .ext-send {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--at-accent);
    color: var(--at-on-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .ext-send:hover {
    background: var(--at-accent-hover);
    color: var(--at-on-accent);
  }

  .ext-note {
    margin-block-end: 0;
    font-size: var(--at-font-size-sm);
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
